Upstream-Name: wiz3D
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/effcol/wiz3D
Source: https://github.com/danielcamposramos/wiz3D (branch partner/wiz3d-proton, fork of https://github.com/effcol/wiz3D, upstream tag v0.3.1)
Comment: wiz3D is derived from the iZ3D stereo driver (https://github.com/bo3b/iZ3D).
 iZ3D Inc.'s code, Copyright (C) iZ3D Inc. 2002 - 2010, was open-sourced under
 the MIT License by its developers through Bo3b Johnson in 2020, and
 /usr/share/doc/wiz3d/LICENSE-iZ3D.txt is that notice verbatim. The wiz3D
 developers' work (effcol and contributors) is under the GNU Lesser General
 Public License, version 2.1: /usr/share/doc/wiz3d/LICENSE.
 .
 The DLLs are cross-built with clang-cl and lld-link against the Windows SDK,
 the MSVC runtime and ATL, fetched by xwin at build time (see
 /usr/share/doc/wiz3d/fetched.txt). Those downloads are not shipped, but the
 static runtime and ATL code the linker takes from them is part of the DLLs.
 Third-party libraries linked statically from ThirdPartyLibs/ and lib/ are
 listed below and in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. This package has not had a
 complete third-party redistribution audit.

